const SAMPLE_MANUAL=`Building description — Citadines Trafalgar Square, London (from GreenGen energy audit, December 2024)
Apart-hotel, 187 guestrooms (126 studios, 49 single, 12 double). Basement plant rooms and an enclosed car park, ground floor reception, breakfast area and lounge, eight guestroom floors.
Gross floor area: 7,280 m². Built before 1960, fully refurbished in 1996.
Occupied hours: 00:00 to 24:00, daily (24/7 hotel operation).
Energy: 100% electricity. 2023 consumption 1,731,400 kWh, 238 kWh/m² per year, 82% above the Ascott energy target of 131.32 kWh/m². Electricity rate £0.27/kWh.
End-use split: space heating 49%, domestic hot water 24%, cooling 5%, catering 4%, plug loads 4%, AHU fans 3%, FCU fans 2%, lighting 2%, office 2%, lifts 1%.
Cooling: one air-cooled Daikin EWAQ400F chiller (407 kW cooling, 154 kW input), installed 2018, serving all guestrooms and common areas. The chiller is controlled locally at the machine only and is not under BMS control.
Guestrooms: one fan coil unit per room with a cooling coil and an electric resistance heater. No mechanical fresh-air supply to guestrooms; room air is recirculated through the FCU. Guestroom toilets have electric radiators.
Guestroom heating setpoint: 21 °C. Some setpoints are too high and equipment run hours are set to 24 h; some filter faults were found.
Common areas: VES AHU with EC motors and heat recovery supplies the breakfast, lounge and restaurant areas. The DX heating coil of the AHU was found switched off; the AHU heats with electric resistance instead.
Outside air: fixed supply from the VES AHU to common areas only, no CO2 or demand-controlled ventilation.
Extract: central guestroom bathroom extract fan runs continuously; common-area, car park and plant-room extract fans are original, without EC motors and without any control.
Domestic hot water: 124 individual electric water heaters (3 kW, 150–250 L) run continuously on manual thermostats.
Lighting: LED throughout; guestrooms on keycard, corridors and stairs on PIR sensors.
BMS: old BMS monitors the chiller and the ventilation units only; no sub-metering, no weather compensation and no fixed time schedule start. No optimum start.
Maintenance: the chiller is well maintained; filter faults were observed on the ventilation units.
Energy reviewed annually by audit against the Ascott target; no energy KPIs tracked in the BMS.
No renewable energy on site.`;

